<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
        <artifactId>qits-ci</artifactId>
        <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <!-- The ci-daemon control-socket wire contract: plain records + enums + the shared type/field
         name constants, framework-free and dependency-free. No JSON library on purpose — each side
         serializes with whatever it already carries (Jackson here, a Vert.x JsonObject in the
         native `ci-daemon` binary).

         VENDORED COPY. The canonical source is
         qits-ci-daemon/ci-daemon-protocol (this repo's sibling submodule). It is copied rather
         than depended on because that module is published to no registry, and a clone of qits-ci
         alone must `mvn verify` green — no GitHub Packages credentials, no prior `mvn install` in
         another repo, no recursive submodule checkout dragging a GraalVM native build into this
         reactor. The same arrangement qits-workspaces has with workspace-daemon-protocol; this is
         knowingly the third such mirrored pair (finish-ci-feature.md §4 decision 3 says so out
         loud rather than letting it accumulate quietly).

         Three things keep the copy honest:
           - The java PACKAGE is identical (eu.wohlben.qits.cidaemon.protocol), so the day this
             artifact is published somewhere, deleting this module and adding a <dependency> is a
             one-line change with no source edits.
           - The artifactId is NOT identical — qits-ci-daemon-protocol under a different groupId —
             so the two jars can never collide in ~/.m2 or on one classpath.
           - CiDaemonCodecTest travels with it. It is the contract test and it runs on both sides;
             a drift in either repo fails a build rather than a socket at runtime.

         THIS COPY IS NEVER EDITED HERE. The daemon repo owns the contract: a change lands there,
         bumps CiDaemonProtocol.CAPABILITY_VERSION, and is re-copied whole. `diff -r` against
         ../../../daemons/qits-ci-daemon/ci-daemon-protocol/src is the drift detector. A "small
         fix" applied to this side instead is exactly how the workspace pair drifted once already
         (migration-plan.md §9 item 19). -->
    <artifactId>qits-ci-daemon-protocol</artifactId>
    <name>qits-ci :: daemon-protocol (vendored)</name>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
